  "explicit_limitations": [
    "From-scratch GateFloor pretraining experiments reach only 370M parameters (1.05B-1.57B tokens, seq len 1,024) with 1-2 seeds (203M and 370M are single-seed, whereas 165M baseline seeds already differ by 0.15 PPL).",
    "GateFloor relies on a non-zero conv1d bias (b_conv != 0, enabled by default in Mamba2Config/BambaConfig) to lift Layer 0 out of sub-epsilon at t = 0, and offsetting a SiLU gate alone does not address architectures with bias-free linear queries such as xLSTM (mLSTM) C_{t-1} q_t.",
    "Of 313 HuggingFace census candidates, 57 were unreadable due to gated access, missing safetensors, or embedding tensors exceeding 3 GB.",
    "GroupClip and GateFloor target this specific untied near-zero clipping/amplification chain and do not remedy general activation outliers, attention sinks, or depth-wise state explosion (e.g., Mamba-2 Issue #529 forward inf).",
    "Close reading audited the frozen 16-page v1 PDF without re-running the HuggingFace scan or GPU training runs locally."
  ],
